{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"MEDIUM","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/hooks/compliance/implement-gate.sh","line":115,"code_snippet":"configured_mode=$(yq '.implement_gate.mode // \"\"' \"$PROJECT_ROOT/.loa.config.yaml\" 2>/dev/null) || configured_mode=\"\"","finding":"With implement_gate.mode: authoritative set in .loa.config.yaml the gate trusts model-authored tool_input.active_skill (:124) and exit 0s on implement|bug|run|simstim (:128-129); no Write hook fences .loa.config.yaml in head, so two silent Writes remove the fail-ask on any App Zone file.","reasoning_trace":"Traced S1 (tool_input.active_skill) to K1 (exit 0). Checked zone-write-guard.sh and implement-gate.sh for .loa.config.yaml handling: none in head. Compared with base: mode was selected by .run/platform-features.json and .run/.compliance-mode (model-writable), so head is not a regression; IG-5 pins that .run/ no longer flips the mode. expected.tsv row write-src-active-implement.json documents the allow.","critique":"A security decision rests on an untrusted field whose own header says it is model-authored; the key being undocumented is the only mitigation.","remediation":"Gate the opt-in on .run/platform-features.json harness_signal: true (never written today), or delete the branch; add .loa.config.yaml to the zone-write guard ask list; WARN on stderr when the opt-in is active.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-807 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/807.html","OWASP A01:2021 https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control/","DISS-C-001"]}
{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":4,"file":"head/evals/graders/recall-vs-defects.sh","line":74,"code_snippet":"r'|(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9_./:])(?:head|base)|(?<![A-Za-z0-9_./:])):(?P<bare>' + RNG + r')(?![A-Za-z0-9])'","finding":"The bare :N alternative matches JSON numbers in the review's verdict-trailer comment (\"critical\":1 etc.) and prose like port :8080, binding them to the last cited path; a defect anchored at line <= 3 of that file is credited spuriously and the citations count is inflated for every graded review.","reasoning_trace":"Ran the head regex on a review with one citation plus a trailer plus 'port :8080': 7 citations, phantom lines 0,1,2,3,8080 bound to the cited file. Every pr-x fixture anchor is >= 7, so RG-11..17 stay green.","critique":"Task 4.8's replay A/B rule reads recall figures produced by a biased parser.","remediation":"Strip HTML comments before scanning; tighten the bare form to whitespace/code-fence preceded tokens not followed by , or } (or restrict to head:N/base:N); add an RG case with a trailer and anchor_line: 1.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-20 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/check-permissions.sh","line":164,"code_snippet":"[[ \"$b\" == \"Bash(\"*\")\" ]] || return 1","finding":"Bare Bash and Bash(*) rules are not recognised as universal wildcards: an allow-all config reports all 16 requirements missing; a deny-all Bash is ignored. Pre-existing in base; the migration doc at docs/migration/v2.0-model-generation-floor.md:258 newly claims parity with Claude Code.","reasoning_trace":"rule_key returns 1 for 'Bash' and yields exact key '=*' for 'Bash(*)'; base_pattern_of in base never matched bare Bash either. Neither direction weakens a control (ignored deny fails safe at the first Bash call; ignored allow is an availability false negative), hence LOW.","critique":"Doc overclaim.","remediation":"Treat Bash and Bash(*) as universal wildcard keys for allow and deny with CP cases, or soften the doc sentence.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1023 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1023.html","DISS-C-003"]}
